<ContentLayout
  title="Watch Multiple Twitch Streams at Once | Stream Mix"
  description="Watch multiple Twitch channels and chats at once in a draggable, resizable browser grid with Stream Mix."
  heading="Watch multiple Twitch streams at once"
  platform="twitch"
>
  <p>
    Stream Mix lets you place several Twitch channels in one customizable grid.
    This is useful for tournaments with multiple player perspectives, watch
    parties, speedrunning events, and creators covering the same live event.
  </p>
  <h2>Add a Twitch channel</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Copy the Twitch channel URL and paste it into Stream Mix.</li>
    <li>Alternatively, choose Twitch and enter only the channel name.</li>
    <li>Select video and chat, video only, or chat only.</li>
    <li>Add more channels, then drag and resize their windows.</li>
  </ol>
  <h2>Twitch embed limitations</h2>
  <p>
    Stream Mix uses Twitch’s official embedded experiences. A channel must be
    available for embedding, and chat or account features can depend on Twitch
    authentication, browser privacy settings, and Twitch service availability.
    Each active player also consumes bandwidth and system resources.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can also <a href="/guides/watch-multiple-streams"
      >mix Twitch with YouTube and Kick</a
    >
    in the same layout.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a href="/" class="btn btn-primary">Open the Twitch multistream viewer</a>
  </p>
</ContentLayout>
